    "is_free": true,
    "controller_support": "full",
    "detailed_description": "<i>Experience the thrill of driving a soapbox car down a mountain in this chaotic cult classic kart racer, accidentally knocking your competitors into the sea or getting lost in green fields without as much as a road sign to help you find your way.</i><br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2899320/extras/67309e1bf42f51c07ad347707e74ccf9.poster.avif?t=1728563585\" width=600 height=196 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2899320/extras/67309e1bf42f51c07ad347707e74ccf9.webm?t=1728563585\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2899320/extras/67309e1bf42f51c07ad347707e74ccf9.mp4?t=1728563585\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Actual features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Physics-based multiplayer kart racing!<br></li><li> Up to 12 players over the Internet or local network<br></li><li> 1-4 local players split screen (online or offline)<br></li><li> Share-a-gamepad option for up to 4 players using 2 game pads</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Questionable features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> 3 large seaside maps (no more, no less)<br></li><li> Randomly generated avatars (you can switch but not choose)<br></li><li> Possible to get lost (the game doesn't even know where to go)<br></li><li> Unpredictable respawn logic (that makes it possible to reach tricky places)<br></li><li> No placement indicator</li></ul><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2899320/extras/ff9a4ddb41ace559795a64b59d8b61d1.poster.avif?t=1728563585\" width=600 height=196 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2899320/extras/ff9a4ddb41ace559795a64b59d8b61d1.webm?t=1728563585\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2899320/extras/ff9a4ddb41ace559795a64b59d8b61d1.mp4?t=1728563585\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Cult classic</h2>This is a remastered version of the original Seaside Racing that was released on Xbox Live Indie Games in 2010.<br><br>The original game has a cult following among <i>at least</i> one group of friends in Indiana, USA, since its original release on Xbox Live Indie Games in 2010. Since publishing this, I\u2019ve also been notified that there is a cult following in High Wycombe, England, UK in addition to the aforementioned cult following in the USA.",
    "about_the_game": "<i>Experience the thrill of driving a soapbox car down a mountain in this chaotic cult classic kart racer, accidentally knocking your competitors into the sea or getting lost in green fields without as much as a road sign to help you find your way.</i><br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2899320/extras/67309e1bf42f51c07ad347707e74ccf9.poster.avif?t=1728563585\" width=600 height=196 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2899320/extras/67309e1bf42f51c07ad347707e74ccf9.webm?t=1728563585\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2899320/extras/67309e1bf42f51c07ad347707e74ccf9.mp4?t=1728563585\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Actual features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Physics-based multiplayer kart racing!<br></li><li> Up to 12 players over the Internet or local network<br></li><li> 1-4 local players split screen (online or offline)<br></li><li> Share-a-gamepad option for up to 4 players using 2 game pads</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Questionable features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> 3 large seaside maps (no more, no less)<br></li><li> Randomly generated avatars (you can switch but not choose)<br></li><li> Possible to get lost (the game doesn't even know where to go)<br></li><li> Unpredictable respawn logic (that makes it possible to reach tricky places)<br></li><li> No placement indicator</li></ul><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2899320/extras/ff9a4ddb41ace559795a64b59d8b61d1.poster.avif?t=1728563585\" width=600 height=196 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2899320/extras/ff9a4ddb41ace559795a64b59d8b61d1.webm?t=1728563585\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2899320/extras/ff9a4ddb41ace559795a64b59d8b61d1.mp4?t=1728563585\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Cult classic</h2>This is a remastered version of the original Seaside Racing that was released on Xbox Live Indie Games in 2010.<br><br>The original game has a cult following among <i>at least</i> one group of friends in Indiana, USA, since its original release on Xbox Live Indie Games in 2010. Since publishing this, I\u2019ve also been notified that there is a cult following in High Wycombe, England, UK in addition to the aforementioned cult following in the USA.",
